{
  "track": "find",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "find-name",
      "title": "Finding files by name",
      "before": "find-01-by-name",
      "summary": "find searches a folder and everything below it.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "text": "Projects grow fast: a few runs, each with its own folders, and soon you can't remember where a file went. `ls` only shows one folder at a time. `find` looks in a folder and every folder inside it."
        },
        {
          "command": {
            "name": "find",
            "stands": "find files",
            "syntax": "find WHERE -name \"PATTERN\"",
            "what": "Searches WHERE and everything below it, and prints the path of every file whose name matches. WHERE is often `.` (here) or `~` (your whole home folder)."
          }
        },
        {
          "try": {
            "text": "Find `il7r_target.pdb` somewhere in your home folder.",
            "cwd": "~",
            "files": {
              "~/binder_design/inputs/il7r_target.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/inputs/notes.txt": "use chain A\n",
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/design_1.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/design_2.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/seqs.fasta": {
                "lib": "fasta:designs"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/design_1.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small",
                "age": "3d"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/seqs.fasta": {
                "lib": "fasta:designs",
                "age": "3d"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/big_traj.dcd": {
                "lib": "text:readme",
                "size": "420M"
              }
            },
            "check": {
              "ran": "find",
              "argHas": "il7r_target.pdb"
            },
            "hint": "find ~ -name \"il7r_target.pdb\"",
            "solution": [
              "find ~ -name \"il7r_target.pdb\""
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "find prints paths relative to WHERE: searching `~` prints `/home/student/binder_design/inputs/il7r_target.pdb`, and that folder is where you `cd` to."
        },
        {
          "quiz": {
            "q": "`find . -name seqs.fasta` prints `./runs/run2/seqs.fasta`. Where is the file?",
            "options": [
              "In your home folder",
              "In runs/run2, below the folder you're in",
              "At the root",
              "Nowhere: . means nothing found"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "why": "`.` is the folder you searched from, so the file is in runs/run2 inside it."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "wildcards",
      "title": "Wildcards: * and ?",
      "before": "find-02-wildcard",
      "summary": "Match many names at once.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "text": "A wildcard stands for characters you don't want to type. The shell expands it into every matching name before the command runs."
        },
        {
          "flags": [
            [
              "*",
              "any characters",
              "`*.pdb` matches every name ending in .pdb; `design_*` every name starting with design_"
            ],
            [
              "?",
              "exactly one character",
              "`design_?.pdb` matches design_1.pdb but not design_10.pdb"
            ],
            [
              "[12]",
              "one of these",
              "`run[12]` matches run1 and run2"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "try": {
            "text": "In run1, list only the PDB files.",
            "cwd": "~/binder_design/runs/run1",
            "files": {
              "~/binder_design/inputs/il7r_target.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/inputs/notes.txt": "use chain A\n",
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/design_1.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/design_2.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/seqs.fasta": {
                "lib": "fasta:designs"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/design_1.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small",
                "age": "3d"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/seqs.fasta": {
                "lib": "fasta:designs",
                "age": "3d"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/big_traj.dcd": {
                "lib": "text:readme",
                "size": "420M"
              }
            },
            "check": {
              "ran": "ls",
              "lineHas": "*.pdb"
            },
            "hint": "ls *.pdb",
            "solution": [
              "ls *.pdb"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "warn": "With find, put the pattern in quotes: `find . -name \"*.pdb\"`. Without them, the shell expands `*.pdb` first, using only the files in the folder you're in, and find gets the wrong question."
        },
        {
          "try": {
            "text": "From `binder_design`, find every PDB in every folder below.",
            "cwd": "~/binder_design",
            "files": {
              "~/binder_design/inputs/il7r_target.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/inputs/notes.txt": "use chain A\n",
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/design_1.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/design_2.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/seqs.fasta": {
                "lib": "fasta:designs"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/design_1.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small",
                "age": "3d"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/seqs.fasta": {
                "lib": "fasta:designs",
                "age": "3d"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/big_traj.dcd": {
                "lib": "text:readme",
                "size": "420M"
              }
            },
            "check": {
              "ran": "find",
              "lineHas": "*.pdb"
            },
            "hint": "find . -name \"*.pdb\"",
            "solution": [
              "find . -name \"*.pdb\""
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "quiz": {
            "q": "Which pattern matches `seqs_A.fasta` and `seqs_B.fasta` but not `seqs_AB.fasta`?",
            "options": [
              "seqs_*.fasta",
              "seqs_?.fasta",
              "*.fasta",
              "seqs.fasta"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "why": "? matches exactly one character, so seqs_AB.fasta (two characters) doesn't match. * would match all three."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tests",
      "title": "Narrowing the search, and counting",
      "before": "find-04-all-fasta",
      "summary": "Only files or only folders, see every folder at once, and count results with a pipe.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "text": "`ls -R` (recursive) lists a folder and every folder inside it, one block per folder. Fine for a small tree; for a big one, find is easier to read."
        },
        {
          "text": "find takes tests after WHERE. Each test narrows the results; give several and a file must pass them all."
        },
        {
          "flags": [
            [
              "-name \"*.fasta\"",
              "name",
              "Name matches the pattern (case matters)"
            ],
            [
              "-iname \"*.PDB\"",
              "name, ignore case",
              "Same, but upper and lower case match each other"
            ],
            [
              "-type f",
              "type: file",
              "Only files"
            ],
            [
              "-type d",
              "type: directory",
              "Only folders"
            ],
            [
              "-maxdepth 1",
              "maximum depth",
              "Don't go more than 1 level down"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "To count results, send find's output into `wc -l` (word count, lines only) with a pipe `|`. The pipe takes everything the first command prints and feeds it to the second, so `wc -l` counts the lines: one per file found."
        },
        {
          "try": {
            "text": "Count the FASTA files below `binder_design`.",
            "cwd": "~/binder_design",
            "files": {
              "~/binder_design/inputs/il7r_target.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/inputs/notes.txt": "use chain A\n",
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/design_1.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/design_2.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/seqs.fasta": {
                "lib": "fasta:designs"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/design_1.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small",
                "age": "3d"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/seqs.fasta": {
                "lib": "fasta:designs",
                "age": "3d"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/big_traj.dcd": {
                "lib": "text:readme",
                "size": "420M"
              }
            },
            "check": {
              "all": [
                {
                  "ran": "wc"
                },
                {
                  "ran": "find",
                  "lineHas": "fasta"
                }
              ]
            },
            "hint": "find . -name \"*.fasta\" | wc -l",
            "solution": [
              "find . -name \"*.fasta\" | wc -l"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "try": {
            "text": "List only the folders below `binder_design`.",
            "cwd": "~/binder_design",
            "files": {
              "~/binder_design/inputs/il7r_target.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/inputs/notes.txt": "use chain A\n",
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/design_1.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/design_2.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/seqs.fasta": {
                "lib": "fasta:designs"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/design_1.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small",
                "age": "3d"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/seqs.fasta": {
                "lib": "fasta:designs",
                "age": "3d"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/big_traj.dcd": {
                "lib": "text:readme",
                "size": "420M"
              }
            },
            "check": {
              "ran": "find",
              "lineHas": "-type d"
            },
            "hint": "find . -type d",
            "solution": [
              "find . -type d"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "quiz": {
            "q": "What does `find . -type d -name outputs | wc -l` print?",
            "options": [
              "The files inside every outputs folder",
              "The number of folders named outputs",
              "The size of outputs",
              "The word outputs"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "why": "find lists folders (-type d) named outputs, one per line, and wc -l counts the lines."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "grep-r",
      "title": "Searching inside files",
      "before": "find-06-grep-id",
      "summary": "When you know what's in the file but not its name.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "command": {
            "name": "grep",
            "stands": "global regular expression print",
            "syntax": "grep [OPTIONS] TEXT FILES",
            "what": "Prints every line in FILES that contains TEXT. The Read files track covers grep in depth; here it's used to find which file holds something."
          }
        },
        {
          "flags": [
            [
              "-r",
              "recursive",
              "Search every file in a folder and its subfolders"
            ],
            [
              "-l",
              "list file names",
              "Print only the names of files that match, not the lines"
            ],
            [
              "-i",
              "ignore case",
              "ERROR, error and Error all match"
            ],
            [
              "-n",
              "line numbers",
              "Show the line number of each match"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "try": {
            "text": "Which file in `binder_design` mentions `chain A`?",
            "cwd": "~/binder_design",
            "files": {
              "~/binder_design/inputs/il7r_target.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/inputs/notes.txt": "use chain A\n",
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/design_1.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/design_2.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/seqs.fasta": {
                "lib": "fasta:designs"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/design_1.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small",
                "age": "3d"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/seqs.fasta": {
                "lib": "fasta:designs",
                "age": "3d"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/big_traj.dcd": {
                "lib": "text:readme",
                "size": "420M"
              }
            },
            "check": {
              "ran": "grep",
              "flags": "r"
            },
            "hint": "grep -r \"chain A\" .",
            "solution": [
              "grep -r \"chain A\" ."
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "quiz": {
            "q": "You want just the names of the log files that contain `out of memory`. Which command?",
            "options": [
              "grep out of memory *.log",
              "grep -l \"out of memory\" *.log",
              "find -name \"out of memory\"",
              "ls *.log"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "why": "-l prints only file names, and the quotes keep the three words together as one search text."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "age-size",
      "title": "Finding by age and size",
      "before": "find-07-today",
      "summary": "What changed recently, and what's eating your space.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "flags": [
            [
              "-mtime -1",
              "modified time",
              "Changed less than 1 day ago (+7: more than 7 days ago)"
            ],
            [
              "-mmin -30",
              "modified minutes",
              "Changed less than 30 minutes ago"
            ],
            [
              "-size +100M",
              "size",
              "Bigger than 100 MB (k, M, G; -10k means smaller than 10 KB)"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "try": {
            "text": "Find the PDB files below `binder_design` that changed in the last day.",
            "cwd": "~/binder_design",
            "files": {
              "~/binder_design/inputs/il7r_target.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/inputs/notes.txt": "use chain A\n",
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/design_1.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/design_2.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/seqs.fasta": {
                "lib": "fasta:designs"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/design_1.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small",
                "age": "3d"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/seqs.fasta": {
                "lib": "fasta:designs",
                "age": "3d"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/big_traj.dcd": {
                "lib": "text:readme",
                "size": "420M"
              }
            },
            "check": {
              "ran": "find",
              "lineHas": "-mtime"
            },
            "hint": "find . -name \"*.pdb\" -mtime -1",
            "solution": [
              "find . -name \"*.pdb\" -mtime -1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "try": {
            "text": "Find anything in your home folder bigger than 100 MB.",
            "cwd": "~",
            "files": {
              "~/binder_design/inputs/il7r_target.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/inputs/notes.txt": "use chain A\n",
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/design_1.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/design_2.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run1/seqs.fasta": {
                "lib": "fasta:designs"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/design_1.pdb": {
                "lib": "pdb:small",
                "age": "3d"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/seqs.fasta": {
                "lib": "fasta:designs",
                "age": "3d"
              },
              "~/binder_design/runs/run2/big_traj.dcd": {
                "lib": "text:readme",
                "size": "420M"
              }
            },
            "check": {
              "ran": "find",
              "lineHas": "-size"
            },
            "hint": "find ~ -size +100M",
            "solution": [
              "find ~ -size +100M"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "tip": "Your home folder has a quota. When it fills up, jobs fail in odd ways. `find ~ -size +100M` is the quickest way to find the culprits; move big data to /scratch."
        },
        {
          "quiz": {
            "q": "Which finds files changed in the last 2 hours?",
            "options": [
              "find . -mtime -2",
              "find . -mmin -120",
              "find . -size -2h",
              "find . -mtime +2"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "why": "-mmin counts minutes, so -120 means less than 120 minutes ago. -mtime counts whole days."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}